# Who may sign an AerieOS release (R199): ssh-keygen's allowed signers
# format, one line a key, and the namespace says for which channel:
#   aerieos-dev namespaces="aerieos-dev" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#   aerieos-release namespaces="aerieos-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... aerieos-release
# Every file an install takes from a release (the controller's bundle,
# AerieOS's image, a stick's image, the apps the Library offers) must be in
# the release's SHA256SUMS, and that list signed by a key here, as the
# install holds this file: the sha256 beside a file is the release's word
# for itself, and whoever can replace a file there can replace that too.
# The release's TAG picks who may have signed. A pre-release (vX.Y.Z-dev.N,
# -rc.N, -beta.N) takes a list signed in either namespace; a stable release
# (vX.Y.Z) takes aerieos-release alone, so the key the release build holds
# can never sign one. A release whose list is unsigned, or signed in a
# namespace its tag may not use, is refused. With no key here at all an
# update of a controller on a machine of its own takes nothing
# (nodes/install-controller.sh): every tree ships this file.
#
# Dev builds publish by themselves, so their signer is the key the release
# build holds (its secret AERIEOS_RELEASE_KEY) and its spare:
# config/aerieos-release.pub's keys as OpenSSH public keys, written here by
# tools/release-signers.py --write and never typed (aerie lint holds them).
aerieos-dev namespaces="aerieos-dev" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIC65rdjAZZY0ad55f/HT6WeaGdkEyTlWSH9eJVDZgugY
aerieos-dev namespaces="aerieos-dev" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFmZ+JSPAxCTUn43jmUEv0NugpMoNa6rzhLWAxY0WGzo
#
# Stable releases are signed by their key's holder on their own machine
# (tools/release-sign.py sign); that private half never touches the
# repository, CI or a controller. Its line goes under this comment, as
# tools/release-sign.py key prints it, committed by hand. Until it is here
# no stable release is taken, and an update to one says no stable signer is
# named yet.
